## Sample bias — this number is optimistic

**The three goals probed are among the four best-documented in the entire corpus.** The rich
`docs/<task>-constitutional-review.md` series — CER-4 six questions + Adversary pass +
recorded Founder verdict — exists for **B0.0–B0.3 only**. From B0.4 onward the sole
close-out artifact is `reviews/tasks/<task>_review.md`, whose 10-point checklist has no
alternatives section and (until B2.x reintroduces an "Adversary / property pass") no
adversary section.

Extrapolating the observed field dependencies to the ~40 later sealed goals suggests a
corpus-wide loss materially above 0.134. That figure is **an estimate, not a measurement** —
this probe measured three goals, and says so. **0.134 is a floor.**

---

## Verdict

verdict: GO

**A8 is confirmed in its diagnosis and refuted in its pessimistic corollary.**

A8 states: *"PAEOS produces all the required artifacts … but as prose documents, not as
typed emission bundles. Carried: if L15 artifacts prove too unstructured to extract
losslessly, S1 fails and Ω1's value is overstated."*

The prose is **not** too unstructured. It is structured by templates that are de-facto
schemas — PAEOS-8 §10's five columns, the Atlas's six columns, CER-4's six questions,
`ledger/debt/README.md`'s six required fields. Hand-extraction recovered **0.866** of the
field inventory with no tooling. Four of eight node types extract at ≥ 0.875; two at 1.000.
`Decision.constitutional_basis`, the field that distinguishes a governed producer from any
other corpus, is 3/3.

The 0.134 loss is a **corpus-completeness** fact, not a schema-viability fact. S1's exit
criterion (§8) is *"a sealed PAEOS goal produces a valid bundle; round-trip is lossless"* —
round-trip losslessness is bundle → store → bundle, which none of these findings threatens.
Every loss identified is fixable by changing what PAEOS emits going forward, at the source,
not by abandoning the design.

**GO is conditional.** Three conditions are blocking for S2's only method:

| # | Condition | Blocks | Owner node |
|---|---|---|---|
| **C1** | Correct §6.1b's source list: add `ledger/debt/`, `docs/<task>-constitutional-review.md`, `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_ATLAS.md`, PAEOS-8 §10 rows. Mark decision-graph / L06 matrix / L04 set as non-existent-at-v1. | F-BUNDLE | `F-BUNDLE` |
| **C2** | Make `Option(rejected)` + `rejection_reason` **mandatory emitted fields** at L06/L15 going forward. Without it `tradeoff_precedents` returns empty for every clean goal. | S2 benefit | lifecycle amendment + `F-BUNDLE` |
| **C3** | Either drop `Scar` from the S1 bundle, or block S1 on populating the scar-graph. Emitting Scar nodes with `detection_signature: null` produces nodes no consumer can match. | S1 validity | `F-BUNDLE` |

| # | Condition (non-blocking, must be honoured in schema) | Owner node |
|---|---|---|
| **C4** | `EvidenceRef.hash` must carry B0.7's bound `artifact_hash` for goals sealed after B0.7. For the historical corpus it must be tagged `recomputed_at_ingest` and **never** presented as the sealed hash. | `F-ENVELOPE` |
| **C5** | `provenance.origin.run_id` must be nullable — it is permanently absent for the pre-Phase-3 corpus. | `F-ENVELOPE` |
| **C6** | Register a **closed** coordinate dimension set (`trust_zone`, `clause`, `phase`, `wave`) or drop `coordinates` from v1. Unbounded dimensions are not conformance-testable (§5.3). | `F-ENVELOPE` |
| **C7** | Decide whether S1's bundle carries `Outcome`. The debt ledger already holds realized outcomes (F6); an S1 without an Outcome slot discards them. | `F-BUNDLE` / S3 scope |

**Recommendation to `G-S1-GO` (founder, A4).** PROCEED, with C1–C3 folded into `F-BUNDLE`
before `I-EXTRACT` starts, and C4–C6 into `F-ENVELOPE`. Per CER-5 this probe recommends and
does not legislate; the disposition is the founder's.

**What would flip this to NO-GO.** Re-running the probe on three goals **without** debt
entries (candidates: B1.C, B2.A, B2.O). If loss there exceeds ~0.35, F2 is fatal rather than
correctable: it would mean the corpus only records decisions when something went wrong, and
`tradeoff_precedents` has no substrate for the normal case. **This is the single highest-value
follow-up and it is cheap** — the same method, three more goals.

